From 704077ab5e9678b9fe60993623bf9775ee952051 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LA <la@LAs-MacBook-Pro.lan>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 21:56:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(deps): regenerate pnpm-lock.yaml to match
 packages/ui/package.json

The Publish workflow has failed every run since 2026-07-31 (5 consecutive,
most recent 2026-08-09 run 31290385310, 16s) at `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`:

    ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE  Cannot install with "frozen-lockfile" because
    pnpm-lock.yaml is not up to date with <ROOT>/packages/ui/package.json
    * 6 dependencies were removed: clsx@^2.1.1, tailwind-merge@^2.6.0,
      zod@^3.25.76, @tailwindcss/cli@^4.1.16, grapesjs@0.23.4, tailwindcss@^4.1.16

packages/ui/package.json on main no longer declares these 6 deps (they were
removed in an earlier commit), but pnpm-lock.yaml was never regenerated to
match in the same commit, so it still carried their stale specifiers. Frozen
install (CI's default) then hard-fails.

Reproduced locally in an isolated worktree at main's tip (3ba97809) before
touching anything, then regenerated: `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile`.
Diff is a clean removal (573 deletions/2 insertions) -- only the packages/ui
importer's specifier list and now-orphaned transitive entries for those 6
(mostly grapesjs/@tailwindcss/cli's own trees); the 2 insertions are an
unrelated `jiti@2.7.0: optional: true` metadata correction. No surviving
package's resolved version changed. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` now
succeeds against this lockfile.

Diagnosis, not fixed here: main is a strict ancestor of general-work (their
merge-base is main's own HEAD) and hasn't been pushed to since 2026-08-09,
while general-work has continued 25+ commits past this point -- the same
"nobody pushes to main" pattern already found in both repos' `ci.yml`. This
fix only makes main's own lockfile internally consistent; it does not decide
whether/when general-work should be merged or fast-forwarded into main, or
whether Publish's `push: branches: [main]` trigger should change the way
ci.yml's did. Changing that trigger has real consequences once NPM_TOKEN is
added (it gates actual `npm publish`, not just test/build), so it is left
for the owner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
